I recently learned that, [according to GitLab][gitlab-ai]:

> "The open-source ethos aligns perfectly with AI in coding, as both are predicated on the principles of community, collaboration and shared innovation."

[gitlab-ai]: https://web.archive.org/web/20260410195115/https://about.gitlab.com/topics/devops/ai-for-coding/

I already (tried to) [give up GitHub](https://sfconservancy.org/GiveUpGitHub/) in 2018, but recently came back to follow the nix and lean communities.

You can now find my most recent work primarily on [codeberg (xhalo32)][codeberg].
I recently [published a nix-based solution](https://codeberg.org/xhalo32/loogle-nix) — enabling Lean and mathlib users to run the [loogle Lean search engine](https://github.com/nomeata/loogle) without friction — following the recent loogle outages.

